WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.943
In tutorial 2.3, you'll connect
Search Console and Google Analytics,

00:00:10.993 --> 00:00:13.143
so your reports use your own figures.

00:00:14.193 --> 00:00:18.393
First, open Website settings,
then Verification & Google.

00:00:18.443 --> 00:00:22.303
Under Google data, click Copy
e-mail to copy the address shown.

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:28.372
Next, in Google Search Console, go to
Settings, then Users and permissions.

00:00:28.422 --> 00:00:31.412
Click Add user, paste the
address, and choose Full.

00:00:31.462 --> 00:00:34.772
Not sure where? Click Show
me how for the exact clicks.

00:00:35.776 --> 00:00:38.726
Then open Google Analytics. It's optional,

00:00:38.776 --> 00:00:42.176
but it adds visits and
conversions to your weekly report.

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:46.501
In Admin, open Property access
management, add the same address,

00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:50.304
and choose the Viewer role. Show
me how has the steps here too.

00:00:51.348 --> 00:00:55.813
Know your property's number? Click
Enter a property ID instead, type it in,

00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:57.211
and click Save ID.

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:04.094
Here's a website with both connected.
Back in Alaventra, click Check again,

00:01:04.144 --> 00:01:06.729
then pick the property
that measures your website.

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:11.249
Search Console shows Connected,
with Full permission.

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:15.987
Now your weekly report, audits and
recommendations use your own Google data.

00:01:16.981 --> 00:01:21.562
So, copy the address, add it in Search
Console, add it in Google Analytics,

00:01:21.612 --> 00:01:22.588
and check again.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.600
Your Google data is connected. Next,
add another website in tutorial 2.4.
